mports could add `copy`.\n\nAlternative: compute truncated body and reconstruct without mutating original, but reimplement Formatter.format logic for prefix. Better use copy.\n\nImplementation:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n    else:\n        r = copy.copy(record)\n        r.message = self._truncate(record.getMessage())  # careful super().format(r) calls getMessage again setting message\n        ...\n```\n\nActually logging.Formatter.format:\n\n```python\nrecord.message = record.getMessage()\nif self.usesTime(): s = self.formatMessage(record)\n...\nif record.exc_info: ...\nif record.stack_info: ...\n```\n\nSo copy record, set copy.msg = truncated message and copy.args = (). Then super().format(copy) yields truncated body and preserves exc_info etc. But requirement budget doesn't include exception traceback or stack_info — copy format appends them full. Good. Also doesn't include prefix. Multi-line alignment uses `record.message` from copy which is truncated message, and msg contains it. Fine.\n\nBut careful: `record.message` might already exist (if formatted before). We make copy and set msg/args. `copy.getMessage()` will set message.\n\n`_truncate`: budget = self.max_message_chars. message = str? getMessage returns str if msg is str; may be non-str if msg not str (e.g. msg object) then formatted via str(msg). `record.getMessage()` returns str(record.msg) if not args... actually if no args, str(msg) only if not isinstance(msg,str)? Let's recall:\n\n```python\ndef getMessage(self):\n    msg = str(self.msg)\n    if self.args:\n        msg = msg % self.args\n    return msg\n```\n\nYes str.\n\nTruncate algorithm: if len(message) <= budget: return. marker = \"...<omitted>...\" length 15. remaining = budget - 15 = 17 for 32. head = ceil(remaining/2) = 9, tail = remaining - head = 8. f\"{message[:head]}{MARKER}{message[-tail:]}\" 